course: dictionary
lesson: 11953
title: Cardinality: how many things are in a group
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cardinality is a maths word for "how many". If you have a group of things, its cardinality is the number of things in that group. Mathematicians call a group a set.
explain: Look at the set of colours red, blue and green. «The cardinality of the set {red, blue, green} is 3.» You can check by counting each thing once: red, blue, green. There are three things, so the cardinality is 3.
explain: Early counting has a key idea called the cardinality principle. «When you count 1, 2, 3, 4, the last number you say tells you how many there are in all.» If you count the apples in a bowl and reach 5, the cardinality of the apples is 5. You do not need to count them all again.
fact: Cardinality means the number of things in a set or group.
fact: A set is a collection of things, such as {red, blue, green}.
fact: «The cardinality of a set» is how many things are in it.
fact: «Cardinality principle» means the last number you count is the total number of things.
fact: Cardinality is always a number, so the cardinality of {red, blue, green} is 3.
exercise: What is the cardinality of the set {cat, dog, fish}? | *3 | 6 | 4 | 2
exercise: Ella counts the pencils in a pot: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6. What is the cardinality of the pencils? | 1 | 3 | 21 | *6
exercise: Which is the best meaning of cardinality? | *The number of things in a set | The name of a group | The biggest number you can count | The colour of a set
test: A bag has 8 marbles. What is the cardinality of the marbles? | 80 | *8 | 9 | 7
test: Sam counts 1, 2, 3, 4 and stops. Using the cardinality principle, how many things are there in all? | *4 | 2 | 1 | 10
exam: The set {2, 4, 6, 8, 10} has how many things in it, so what is its cardinality? | *5 | 6 | 10 | 4
